  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * This fast version uses a 32-bit accumulator with 2.30 format.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * The accumulator maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplication results but provides
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator result overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by two bits and lie 
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 accumulator is then shifted by <code>postShift</code> bits and the result truncated to 
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  *
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
